  "data_abstract": "The STAR Collaboration reports the first observation of exclusive $\\rho^0$ photoproduction, $AuAu\\rightarrow AuAu\\rho^0$, and $\\rho^0$ production accompanied by mutual nuclear Coulomb excitation, $AuAu\\rightarrow Au^\\ast Au^\\ast \\rho^0$, in ultraperipheral heavy-ion collisions. The $\\rho^0$ have low transverse momenta, consistent with coherent coupling to both nuclei. The cross sections at $\\sqrt{s_{_{NN}}}$ = 130 GeV agree with theoretical predictions treating $\\rho^0$ production and Coulomb excitation as independent processes.",
